module gunbc.inference_endpoint_binding

import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import extdeps.time.rfc3339 { Rfc3339Timestamp }

// WHY THIS IS NOT A FIELD ON ProviderInterfaceBinding OR CodexProviderRuntimeReceipt, and why two
// independent searches for it returned a confident zero.
//
// THE CORPUS CARRIES TWO SENSES OF THE WORD "PROVIDER" and they are different subjects:
//   (1) the coding-agent RUNTIME we install and control -- gunbc.provider_interface_binding
//       ProviderInterfaceBinding and gunbc.codex_provider_runtime_receipt
//       CodexProviderRuntimeReceipt. Every field is about HOW A PROCESS IS INSTALLED AND CONTROLLED.
//   (2) the INFERENCE BACKEND that process sends requests to -- upstream's own use of the word, as
//       in codex's `model_providers` config key.
//
// Both carriers in sense (1) have "Provider" in their name and no field ranging over sense (2). So
// searching them for an endpoint is searching the right word in the wrong subject, and the absence
// found there reads as absence everywhere. That happened twice, independently, before anyone noticed
// the homonym.
//
// This module therefore avoids the word in its own name. Putting an endpoint on either carrier above
// would fuse process-control with model-backend -- one carrier answering for another subject.

// GROUNDING OF THIS MODULE, stated on its face so a reader can falsify each type without
// re-deriving the argument. Every type below names an authority OUTSIDE this module that could make
// it wrong today. A type that could only be falsified once a consumer arrives is not modeled here;
// four such types were removed rather than carried (see the removal note at the foot of this file).
//
// The layer is legitimate: extdeps.ollama.api's own scope note assigns "which model, which host,
// which endpoint binding" to gunbc, and keeps only the HTTP API surface for itself.

// THE URL A HARNESS WAS CONFIGURED TO DIAL IS A FACT ABOUT THE MACHINE RUNNING THE HARNESS, not
// about any serving host. Under a direct bind the two coincide and a carrier fusing them looks
// correct forever; the first tunnel, proxy or shared name breaks it silently.
//
// GROUNDED BY: extdeps.ollama.api OllamaEndpoint, referenced symbolically through wire_surface.
//
// wire_surface IS A DeclarationRef AND NOT A PRODUCT ENUM, and that is a §3 requirement rather than
// a style choice. extdeps.ollama.api states that adding vLLM or a NIM container must not widen a
// central product enum -- each serving product is its own module citing its own API. An enum here
// enumerating OllamaNative | OpenAiResponses | AnthropicMessages would be exactly that forbidden
// hub: this module would have to be edited for a product whose authority lives elsewhere. Naming
// the upstream declaration instead means a new backend is a new extdeps module and no edit here.
//
// FALSIFIABLE TODAY: the reference must resolve to a real declaration. Point it at a module or a
// symbol that does not exist and it is wrong immediately, with no consumer required.
type DialledEndpoint {
  url: NonEmptyStr
  wire_surface: DeclarationRef
}

// WHETHER A DIALLED URL REACHED A PARTICULAR HOST IS NOT DERIVABLE FROM THE RESPONSE ON THIS FLEET,
// AND THAT IS A CONSEQUENCE OF CONVERGENCE RATHER THAN A GAP IN THE PROBE.
//
// GROUNDED BY: the srv5/srv6 byte-identical convergence observation carried in
// gunbc.spark.serving_observe and gunbc.spark.serving_terminal_health -- same runtime version, same
// model, same materialization identity, same observation digest. Every fact a response could carry
// is exactly what convergence was built to make identical, so no response can discriminate its
// origin. The property we engineered is what forecloses the question.
//
// FALSIFIABLE TODAY: if those two hosts ever report differing version, model or digest, this type's
// premise is false and JoinObservedFromResponse becomes reachable without any new probe.
//
// So this is NOT an Unobserved arm. An Unobserved arm carries an implicit promise that a better
// probe closes it, and no probe can. It is an ASSERTION, and an assertion has an asserter, a basis
// and a time. On a tunnel the basis is the tunnel's own configuration, which lives on the operator's
// workstation and never enters the response.
//
// NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named so the arm is not an untracked stall: observing the join requires a
// DELIBERATE ASYMMETRY -- a per-host marker the response can carry. That means deliberately
// un-converging something, which is a design decision with a real cost, not a probe improvement.
type EndpointHostJoin
  = JoinAssertedBy {
      asserter: NonEmptyStr
      basis: NonEmptyStr
      asserted_at: Rfc3339Timestamp
    }
  | JoinObservedFromResponse {
      per_host_marker: NonEmptyStr
    }

fn endpoint_host_join_wire(j: EndpointHostJoin) -> String {
  match j {
    JoinAssertedBy { asserter: a, basis: b, asserted_at: t } =>
      join([
        "join=ASSERTED asserter=", a as String, " basis=", b as String, " at=", t as String,
        " -- not observed from the response, and not observable while the fleet is identically converged",
      ], "")
    JoinObservedFromResponse { per_host_marker: m } =>
      join(["join=OBSERVED per_host_marker=", m as String], "")
  }
}

// WHAT WAS REMOVED HERE, AND WHY IT IS NOT PARKED SOMEWHERE.
//
// InferenceWireProtocol, TurnPrecondition<T>, WireSubsetExercised, CodingTurnReceipt and
// TurnReceiptStanding were removed after each was tested against the question this module now
// answers on its face: what outside authority could make this wrong TODAY.
//
// InferenceWireProtocol enumerated OpenAiResponses, OpenAiChatCompletions and AnthropicMessages.
// Measured against the fleet, that closed set was already wrong by omission: extdeps.ollama.api
// models no OpenAI-compatible surface at all, and gunbc.spark.serving_observe probes Ollama's native
// API, so the one wire srv5 and srv6 actually serve was absent from the set. It was also the
// forbidden product hub described above.
//
// The receipt half named no outside authority. Its preconditions and standing were derived shapes,
// and its wire-subset arm distinguished a statefulness axis of a protocol nothing on this fleet
// serves -- falsifiable only once a consumer arrives, which is the definition of a slice.
//
// Its fixtures are the reason the test is worth stating: the dialled port was 127.0.0.1:11435, a
// number with zero occurrences anywhere in this repository outside the module's own witness, while
// the fleet serves 11434; and harness_version was 0.148.0, while gunbc.package_delivery
// codex_required_package_version pins 0.146.0. Both read as measurements because they were
// specific. Neither was measured.
//
// The version was NOT corrected to the pinned value. extdeps.llm.codex_app_server codex_plan_type_note
// records the same defect at 0.147.0 and states the rule: a protocol fact is cited from the exact
// executable the runtime receipt admits, and a bump moves manifest, lock, admitted artifacts and
// receipt together or it does not happen. Rewriting 0.148.0 to 0.146.0 would have made an
// ungrounded field match an authority it was never derived from -- converting a detectable
// fabrication into an undetectable one. A wrong value that matches nothing is a finding; a wrong
// value that matches something is a lie. If a turn receipt returns, its version comes from an
// executable that ran.

// The endpoint surface this fleet's harnesses dial today. A second backend is a second declaration
// beside this one, never a widened enum above.
data ollama_native_wire_surface: DeclarationRef = DeclarationRef {
  module_path: "extdeps.ollama.api",
  decl_name: "OllamaEndpoint",
  field: WholeDeclaration
}
